it was 1944  our orders were to liberate the italian  city of gita  taking the beach was our first objective  shells were raining down on us as we  rushed toward the german fortifications  the german bunkers were overlooking the  entire beach  once we were in range we hit them from  both sides  once the first bunker collapsed the  defense opened up  after securing the beach we were told to  take a nearby flak 88  blowing up the artillery was the only  way we could hold our position  we accomplished our mission but  this long day had just begun  while we led the main front they dropped  in paratroopers to stop any german  reinforcements  they never saw them coming  they never stood a chance  the outskirts of the city were now ours  we set up a forward base urgently  building a triage center for the wounded  we rallied together and prepared for the  final assault  we made our way toward the city square  they were expecting us  but we were one step ahead of them even  with the help from the british  we knew this was going to be an uphill  fight  german troops were gathered in the main  square we didn't expect that level of  resistance  under heavy fire buildings collapsing  around us and for a while  they had the upper hand but we kept on  pushing  we managed to hold the position long  enough for air support to arrive  the city was ours but our fight in italy  had only just begun  [Music]  you
 

